So one of the things that often causes problems for me in the early game
is a lack of poison resistance. Usually I manage to eat something that
gives me poison resistance fairly quickly, but sometimes I don't, and
then I am very nervous descending. The first sign of Uruk-Hai who might
have poisoned arrows and I am off that dungeon level, but sometimes the
first sign is too late. Not to mention poisoned spikes. Therefore I've
been looking for ways to get poison resistance as early as possible,
and this morning I hit on one:

Farm puddings not for their deathdrops, but for their corpses. 

Brown puddings don't always leave corpses, and have a rot attack, but in
the early game you don't want that armor anyway, and they are unable to
do any HP damage no matter how bad your AC is. Each corpse you eat has
an 11% chance of providing poison resistance; you might also get cold
or shock resistance. I happened to have an altar when I did this, so I
prayed up a few golden glows while I was at it, but it's hardly necessary.
Once I got poison and shock resistance (already had cold), I stopped;
pudding farming is boring.

I expect you could do this with black puddings as well, which always
leave corpses and have a 22% chance of giving resistance. I expect it
requires judicious use of Elbereth. I was playing illiterate (it's _so
fun!_ I don't know why I ever bothered with scrolls or spells) and that
wasn't an option for me, but it does imply that you might be able to
get poison resistance right off by kicking a sink...

A couple of problems with this strategy, and how to get around them:

 * Pudding corpses are acidic

   - Have enough HP! 
   - Tinning kit! (Yes, this works, just wizmoded it)
   - ...acid resistance? Alchemy smock, I guess

 * Pudding corpses are 250 nutrition each, making this time-consuming

   - Amulet of magical breathing
   - Ring of hunger
   - Tinning kit! Man, tinning kits are great.
   - Jumping boots or knight intrinsic jumping
   - Spellcasting (if not wizard with INT >16)
   - ...and whatever else people use to deal with becoming non-Satiated

 * Other monsters might walk up to you

   - surround yourself with enough black puddings to stay safe
   - boulders with Elbereth under them
   - do this on DL 1 

This isn't foolproof and won't be the best way to get poison resistance
in every game, but if you find yourself with a pudding and a desire to
get poison resistance before progressing farther, I recommend it. I'd be
interested in hearing suggestions on how to improve this technique or 
alternately better ways to score early poison resistance. 

